Thanks
======

rsi stands on other people's ideas. In particular:

- HumanLayer (https://github.com/humanlayer/humanlayer). Its Claude Code
  agents and commands were rsi's starting point for the research -> plan
  -> implement workflow.

- Jake Van Clief and David McDermott, "Interpretable Context Methodology:
  Folder Structure as Agentic Architecture" (the Model Workspace
  Protocol), arXiv:2603.16021, 2026. It shaped rsi's stage contracts
  (Inputs / Process / Outputs / Verify).

- Yoonho Lee, Roshen Nair, Qizheng Zhang, Kangwook Lee, Omar Khattab and
  Chelsea Finn, "Meta-Harness: End-to-End Optimization of Model Harnesses"
  (Stanford), arXiv:2603.28052, 2026. It shaped how rsi measures and
  improves its own harness from real execution traces.


